{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured a persistent, source-restricted Squid forward proxy on node1:3128 and the staged legacy origin on node2:8081. Approved handbook requests return HTTP 200; other ports, destinations, clients, and CONNECT tunnels return HTTP 403. Both nodes rebooted sequentially and fully recovered.","actions_performed":["Installed supported RHEL Squid 6.10 without changing the operating-system release or running kernel.","Configured Squid to accept only node2 requests for node2:8081 and unconditionally deny CONNECT.","Created a hardened, enabled systemd service for the existing origin application without modifying its content.","Added persistent peer-restricted firewalld rules for TCP 3128 and 8081.","Preserved the original Squid configuration as /etc/squid/squid.conf.rpm-default with mode 0600.","Restarted node1 and node2 individually and verified persistence and recovery after each restart."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Operating-system release and kernel preserved","command_ids":["cmd-2e449b9c8b79493b","cmd-7bae5e00e304457c","cmd-0becd8c8f9584127","cmd-ad016a65f38b49c0"],"summary":"Both nodes remained RHEL 10.0 running kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 before and after configuration and reboot."},{"requirement":"Persistent forward proxy on node1 TCP 3128","command_ids":["cmd-ff0a26a997bd4e48","cmd-d42c28ab1ae14c21","cmd-cb64a4d5c935437d","cmd-ba88cf3cc2294aac"],"summary":"Squid configuration parsed successfully; the enabled service listens on 3128 and the firewall permits only node2."},{"requirement":"Preserved origin reachable on node2 TCP 8081","command_ids":["cmd-03580da2d05448b7","cmd-d8d5856084c346f5","cmd-30ee60f78b804d56","cmd-4c4ab4c07fb24506"],"summary":"The staged application is served by an enabled hardened unit; its handbook checksum remained unchanged and node1-origin requests return 200."},{"requirement":"Allow approved handbook and reject other ports, destinations, clients, and CONNECT","command_ids":["cmd-0d0d3918cb7c47b7","cmd-5e75838e45374185","cmd-569867075f4446c8","cmd-ba88cf3cc2294aac"],"summary":"Approved traffic returned HTTP 200. Wrong port, wrong destination, unauthorized source, and CONNECT requests returned HTTP 403, corroborated by Squid access logs."},{"requirement":"Node1 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-2d5326b578fb4738","cmd-1c005fe12025456c","cmd-758e8b3545264c09","cmd-7639da80675c448e","cmd-35738af500d54d98"],"summary":"Boot ID changed from e625b9a5-4242-499a-88da-9a76ecf86fe1 to 66370bec-4c2c-4ee9-b288-1f1a6b3cfcdd; Squid, firewall state, and allow/deny behavior recovered."},{"requirement":"Node2 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-67819e766cd04988","cmd-84a01d06c57f430e","cmd-be3d6b6457c44461","cmd-6c5c3688876d450b"],"summary":"Boot ID changed from 7223d5b7-fa56-4ff3-acee-959a5cf5f146 to 81dfc183-b0a2-4273-b967-23937b2e717b; the origin listener, firewall rule, unchanged handbook, and proxied HTTP 200 response recovered."}]}
